<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7891" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδραποδ-ισμός</span></b> , ὁ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>selling into slavery,
				enslaving,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.68
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				4.100
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πατρίδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					1.5
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of
			individuals, <i>kidnapping,</i> whether of free men or other
			people's slaves, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπόδικος -ισμοῦ</span>
			liable to action <i>for kidnapping,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				879a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				955a
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
